\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 Fire Worm
\f1\b0\fs24 \
14 days after bombing\
\pard\tx360\tx720\tx1080\tx1440\tx1800\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\pardeftab720\fi360\sl264\slmult1\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f3\fs26 Sarah arrived at work as usual about 30 minutes early to find her little signals-directorate already hard at work. They had been working on cracking scrambled computer records, communications transmissions and had made some significant progress. They had traced a million dead-ends, but had tracked down the source of the covert information adjustment, but \'85\'85\'85\'85\
The algorithms of the surveillance programs had identified a company agent, at an unknown location, who was interrogating the link, trying every possible angle to gather information on Cracker Jack Cleaning services. As the focus of attention from company agent, Cracker had a target on his back and they were closing in fast. She tried desperately to locate where the inquiries had originated, but hadn\'92t had any luck before Supt Lanning interrupted, calling her in for a meeting to discuss progress in the Emil Kalheri conundrum.\cf0 \
\'93The records were deleted by a \'93Sleeping Fire-worm\'94. It\'92s primitive, but effective enough to fool most security systems. I\'92m in the process of clearing the system, but it moves about and hides very well. I don\'92t think it breached the system, I think it was put there as a part of the system. It has always been there.\'94\
\'93What about Mr Kalheri?\'94\
\'93All information about him is lost. He could be anywhere.\'94\
\'93Any idea who is using the fire-worm?\'94\
\'93Yes, as a matter of fact, but you may not like it.\'94\
\'93Who?\'94\
\'93It is used almost exclusively by the Office of the CEO, The Director of Pre-emptive Reciprocity and Proactive Euthanasia and the Office of the Commissioner of Police. The most recent user was our boss. It took 300 solid hours of processing to track down the location to the office next door.\'94\
 \'93That\'92s is a surprise.\'94 She was, in fact, not surprised at all. Every senior official in the Primary Trade Dominion was corrupt and she had no reason to suspect her boss was different. \'93Anything else?\'94\
 \
\'93The Fire-worm was has been used infrequently over the past several months. Personal information is deleted and then the subject disappears with no trace. It was used recently on a no-name cleaner from Sector 3. All records regarding an Anthony Hardy L.2.were deleted from the Commissioner\'92s Desk.\'94 \
\'93Do you think he is connected to our inquiry?\'94\
\'93Perhaps. If he disappears or is killed we will know for sure.\'94 Sarah did not want to give the game away and hoped Hayley would make the suggestion.\
\'93Well, we can\'92t let that happen. I think we should bring him into protective custody and see why the Commissioner finds him so interesting.\'94\
\'93We?\'94\
\'93Yes. You are hereby deputised.\'94 Hayley raised a holo-document from the emitter.\
\'93I don\'92t want to be a cop, I\'92m a privateer. I am happy to lend you my expertise in the office, but I am not an operative.\'94 It would be difficult for Sarah to wash away the stigma of public service.\
\'93Relax, you will still be a private contractor. Shit, you get paid about twice what I am getting and in any case it\'92s compulsory for long term contractors. You can\'92t leave the office otherwise and sometimes your duties will demand go out on operations. Like now for example. Your clearance came through today and you are, from today, a fully operational contractor. Do you know how to shoot?\'94 \
\'93This is the PTD. The only thing we make is weapons. Everyone knows how to shoot.\'94\
\'93Alexander Shakti can\'92t.\'94\
\'93I have heard that.\'94 They both giggled.\
The Commissioner, listening in from the comfort of his office chair, called his secretary. \'93Get me Shakti.\'94\
